# Pull requests

Cloud agents create and update pull requests with the **`ManagePullRequest`** tool only.
Do **not** use `gh pr create`, `gh pr edit`, or other `gh` API commands for PRs — the
Cursor GitHub installation token can push code but returns 403 for most PR/issue API calls.

## Create

1. Commit and push the branch (`git push -u origin <branch>`).
2. Call `ManagePullRequest` with `action: create_pr`, plus `title`, `body`, `branch_name`,
   and `base_branch` (default `main`).
3. Open as **draft** unless the user explicitly asks otherwise (`draft: true` by default).

## Update

After additional commits or before finishing a turn, call `ManagePullRequest` with
`action: update_pr` and `branch_name` (or `pr_url`) to refresh title/body if needed.

## Assignee

Every standard PR should be assigned to **`alexseymer`**. The integration cannot set
assignees via API — mention the assignee in the PR body or turn summary so it can be
applied on GitHub (PR sidebar → Assignees).

## Branch naming

Cloud agent branches use the `cursor/<descriptive-name>-203b` pattern.
